@flexiarg operator/type-the-intent-as-a-prefix-token
@title Type The Intent As A Prefix Token
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-LPN1KW turn-O8dzJL
@parent cycle-machine/step-machine
@context Messages between operator and agent are typed by intent (bells, parks) and the operator wants to type the intent himself.

! conclusion: Start the line with the token and colon so the matcher reads the intent.

  + IF:
    He says he can simulate the typed pipe by starting a line with <token>:, and that it generalises Emacs M-.

  + HOWEVER:
    The prefix may collide with ordinary text, and the pairing must be matched by the reader.

  + THEN:
    Start the line with the token and colon so the matcher reads the intent.

  + BECAUSE:
    The same tokens on both sides make pairing easy and give more modifiers than keys.
